[{"id":3894385048,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7oH5mY","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?u=ec87bf81cd2f5f0947670400f48cf0845c25d719&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested, the overall UX of the feature makes sense.\r\n\r\nIt currently has problems related to mismatch of camera position and cursor:\r\n\r\n1. When you first start orbiting with middle mouse button it snaps to a wrong angle first.\r\n2. If you animate the camera with an AnimationPlayer (a common use for piloting) and try to pilot the camera after scrubbing through the timeline it will snap to a wrong position, ignoring the actual camera position that the animation player has set.\r\n\r\nI also noticed that having to always click two checkboxes when i.e trying to animate two separate cameras quickly gets old. I suggest considering these improvements:\r\n\r\n1. If we're in a camera preview mode, selecting another camera in the scene tree should switch the viewport to the other camera (if we only have one viewport), preserving the state of the piloting checkbox.\r\n2. Maybe there could be a power feature where Shift+clicking the preview checkbox would also enable piloting + a mention of that behavior in the tooltip to make it easier to discover.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109945#pullrequestreview-3894385048","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109945","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109945#pullrequestreview-3894385048"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109945"}},"submitted_at":"2026-03-05T07:18:26Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3908666593,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7o-YTh","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?u=ec87bf81cd2f5f0947670400f48cf0845c25d719&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested, can confirm that the unrelated commit fixes the issue. Also all of the other bugs that I found have been fixed. Approving on UX, this still needs a code review.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109945#pullrequestreview-3908666593","pull_request_url":"https